\title{Yve Meng}
\taxon{Person}
\meta{external}{https://sez.moe/}
\meta{institution}{Thalesians / Mediobanca}
\meta{orcid}{0009-0008-0934-6821}
\meta{position}{they/them}

\p{I am a \em{Quantitative Researcher} in [Mediobanca](https://www.mediobanca.com/en/index.html) in London. I am also a \em{Research Assistant} in [Thalesians](https://thalesians.com/), supervised under [Dr. Paul Bilokon](https://profiles.imperial.ac.uk/paul.bilokon01).}
\p{I am an alumni of \em{MSc Mathematics and Finance} in Imperial College. I am also an alumni of [University of Cambridge](thoughts-emo-0001) as a \em{[Mathmo](https://archive.thetab.com/uk/cambridge/2017/02/16/what-actually-date-mathmo-89152)} \em{(BA Mathematics Tripos)}.}
\p{My primary research interest focuses on algebraic aspects in stochastic analysis. You may find more information on the [research](0008) page. Currently, I am working on a paper formalising market dynamics using a game-theoretical framework, and furthermore, under a game semantical interpretation.}
\p{Previously in Imperial, I was supervised by [Prof. Thomas Cass](https://profiles.imperial.ac.uk/thomas.cass), who had provided me with insights in Rough Path Theory. When I was In Cambridge, I was supervised by [Prof. Simon Wadsley](https://www.dpmms.cam.ac.uk/~sjw47/), [Prof. Anthony Ashton](https://www.homerton.cam.ac.uk/people/anthony-ashton) and [Prof. Martin Hyland](https://www.dpmms.cam.ac.uk/person/jmeh1), and worked on researches generalising semantical correspondences of commutative submonads in ambient categories.}
\p{I use NixOS on my personal devices. I also maintain an Emacs configuration file.}
\p{I am a member of [UK Liberal Democrats](https://www.libdems.org.uk/)}
\p{I currently live in Shoreditch, London. I'll be more than happy if you would like to have a coffee chat with me.}
